Automated processing of LaTeX templates presents a significant challenge in academic document development, particularly when dealing with various templates that have different structures and requirements. This research proposes an AI-based approach to optimize this process, focusing on template structure analysis and appropriate content generation. The methodology combines natural language processing and machine learning techniques to analyze LaTeX templates, identify document structures, and generate content that complies with the required format. The developed system can handle various types of LaTeX templates with an 85% success rate, reducing processing time by up to 70% and improving document format accuracy compared to manual methods. The results demonstrate that the AI-based approach can significantly enhance efficiency and accuracy in LaTeX template processing, opening opportunities for further development in academic document automation.

Keywords: LaTeX, template processing, artificial intelligence, document automation, natural language processing 